  "summary_en": "Arkansas statute (Act 926 of 2021) permitting personal delivery devices, i.e. automated sidewalk delivery robots, in pedestrian areas and on certain roads. It sets speed limits, pedestrian right-of-way, lighting, identification markers and a $100,000 insurance minimum. It exempts the devices from vehicle registration and preempts local regulation of design and insurance.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Max speed 10 mph in pedestrian areas and 20 mph on county/municipal roads; banned on highways and roads over 45 mph",
   "Devices must yield to pedestrians and obey traffic signals",
   "Each device needs an identifying marker and unique number",
   "Operators must carry at least $100,000 general liability insurance per device",
   "Exempt from vehicle registration; localities may ban for safety but cannot regulate design or insurance"
  ],
